-- the medium as chemistry rather than as two flags. A Situation carries whether the medium is chiral and
-- whether it catalyses, and those are the right inputs to the admission test, but they are not facts
-- anyone measures directly: what is measured is what is dissolved. So the mixture is the datum and the
-- flags are computed from it.
--
-- whether any of a species's own symmetries is improper. A molecule is achiral exactly when an improper
-- operation is among its symmetries, and the smallest such operation is a mirror plane that acts as the
-- identity on the atoms -- which is how water and dimethylformamide carry their achirality here. A species
-- with no improper symmetry is chiral.
any-improper : List SMotion → Bool
any-improper qs = case qs of
  nil → false
  cons q r → (case sm-proper q of true → any-improper r; false → true)
